  {
   "line": 5,
   "text": "Here is the picture behind it. A tone is a dot going round a wheel, and its pitch is how far the dot turns between two samples. The whine flips it halfway around, every single time. So put every tone on that wheel, zero hertz on the right, four thousand on the left. The average has one special point, a zero, sitting right where the whine lands.",
